+    brief: Describes one agent authorization/governance decision.
+    note: |
+      `gen_ai.operation.name` SHOULD be `execute_authorization`.
+
+      This span represents a single decision made by the deciding component (a policy decision
+      point, agent gateway, or governance layer in front of an agent action). It is NOT emitted by
+      agent-level or model-call instrumentation, which does not have access to the trust / risk /
+      scan inputs or the authority basis the decision is measured against.
+
+      Structural invariants:
+
+      1. A `gen_ai.execute_authorization` span is present if and only if the gate actually evaluated
+         a decision. If nothing was in the reachable surface, there is no decision and no span; that
+         case is the absence of the operation, not an `outcome` value.
